From: Harshit Gupta <39994376+arelyx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:15:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] st/mesa: lower indirect uniform derefs for ARB programs
 without indirect_const_addr

The GLSL path already lowers indirect uniform derefs to if/else trees
when the driver lacks indirect constant addressing. ARB programs that
index parameters with the address register skipped that step, so a2xx
asserted on a non-constant load_uniform offset (piglit vp-address-01).

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QFJdrUq9L8NDS5PyGFCsG9
---
 src/mesa/state_tracker/st_program.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_program.c b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_program.c
index 058de4c..34ff7d6 100644
--- a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_program.c
+++ b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_program.c
@@ -395,6 +395,14 @@ st_prog_to_nir_postprocess(struct st_context *st, nir_shader *nir,
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_reg_intrinsics_to_ssa);
    nir_validate_shader(nir, "after st/ptn lower_reg_intrinsics_to_ssa");
 
+   /* ARB programs can index parameters with the address register.  Drivers
+    * without indirect constant addressing get the same if/else lowering the
+    * GLSL path applies in st_glsl_to_nir.
+    */
+   if (!screen->shader_caps[nir->info.stage].indirect_const_addr)
+      NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_indirect_derefs_to_if_else_trees,
+               nir_var_uniform, UINT32_MAX);
+
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, st_nir_lower_wpos_ytransform, prog, screen);
    NIR_PASS(_, nir, nir_lower_system_values);
 
